  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is very adventurous, so he asked Bob to give him a task.\n\nBob gave him a sequence of blocks with heights A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. Chef is at the first block and he has to reach the NNN-th block using the minimum number of moves to complete the task.\n\nIn one move, he can jump from the iii-th block to the jjj-th block only if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n\ni&lt;ji \\lt ji&lt;j\nAi≥AjA_i \\geq A_jAi​≥Aj​\nfor all kkk (i&lt;k&lt;ji \\lt k \\lt ji&lt;k&lt;j), Ak≤AjA_k \\leq A_jAk​≤Aj​\nYou have to find the minimum number of moves Chef needs to perform to reach the last block, or determine that it is impossible.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer --- the minimum number of moves or −1-1−1 if it is impossible to reach the last block.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai≤1050 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^50≤Ai​≤105 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (30 points):**",
      "2≤N≤1,0002 \\leq N \\leq 1,0002≤N≤1,000",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1045 \\cdot 10^45⋅104",
      "**Subtask #2 (70 points):** original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5\n9 15 8 13 8\n9\n20 16 13 9 17 11 15 8 7",
        "output": "-1\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: There is no way to move from the first block (with height 999) to any other block.\nExample case 2: The only sequence of 444 moves is 20→17→15→8→720 \\rightarrow 17 \\rightarrow 15 \\rightarrow 8 \\rightarrow 720→17→15→8→7. For example, in the first move, all the heights between 202020 and 171717 do not exceed 171717, so all conditions are satisfied."
      }
    ]
